  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Transplant was created at Asheville Bookworks in West Asheville, North Carolina during a three-month book-arts residnecy with the support of numerous midwives and matron saints. The twelve stories in Transplant are based on memories from twelve of my childhood houses. Each piece of vellum lifts to reveal a story beyond the image presented in the first sentence. The body of Transplant was built with cream Stonehenge, the spines and fly leaves are Strathmore Kimono Red, and the text was printed on a Vandercook proofing press using hand-set 10 point Garamond on peach vellum. The houses were die cut on a Kluge platen press"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Artist's book comprised of twelve folded leaves of heavy cream paper, each sewn across the bottom to form a compartment; the ends of the stitching are several inches long and hang loose. Vellum leaves slide into each compartment and contain a short story on the recto. Each folded leaf also has a cut-out in the shape of a house revealing the first line of text. The paper leaves are attached to heavy red paper to form the spine. Covers are cloth-covered boards with a recessed house shape on the front. Binding is Coptic-style.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Edition of 48 copies, signed by the artist.</subfield>
  </datafield>
